    "title": "WWE WrestleMania 42: How Much It Costs to Watch",
    "text": "WrestleMania 42 is finally here, and for fans watching from home, the biggest question isn’t just who’s on the card—it’s how much it costs to tune in. This year marks a major shift in how WWE’s biggest event is distributed in the United States, with a new streaming home and a different pricing structure than in years past. Here’s everything you need to know about the cost of watching WrestleMania 42. WWE Chief Content Officer Triple H has aggressively expanded the company’s global footprint, turning international “Premium Live Events” into massive revenue drivers.Getty Images In the United States, WrestleMania 42 streams exclusively on ESPN’s direct-to-consumer service, ESPN Unlimited. Standalone subscription: $29.99 per month Bundle options (Disney+, Hulu + ESPN Unlimited): starting around $35.99 per month Unlike the traditional pay-per-view model, there is no separate fee for WrestleMania. Once subscribed, fans can watch both nights of the event at no additional cost. Is WrestleMania 42 Free? Free Trial Options While ESPN Unlimited does not consistently offer a direct free trial, several live TV services that include the platform occasionally run free trial promotions for new users. Providers that are offering free trials this weekend include: FuboTV Hulu + Live TV DIRECTV As with any free trial, pay attention to its length and evaluate if you want to keep the subscription afterwards. Allegiant Stadium in Las Vegas will host WrestleMania for the second year in a row.Getty Images Do You Already Have Access? Not everyone needs to sign up separately. Some cable and live TV providers already include ESPN Unlimited as part of their packages, meaning you may be able to watch WrestleMania 42 simply by logging into the ESPN app. After linking your TV provider to a MyDisney account, the event can be streamed across mobile devices, smart TVs, and web browsers. Here’s Cody Rhodes explaining how to watch WrestleMania: When WrestleMania 42 Starts WrestleMania 42 takes place across two nights: Saturday, April 18, 2026 Sunday, April 19, 2026 Both nights begin at: 6:00 p.m. ET 5:00 p.m. CT 3:00 p.m. PT (Las Vegas local time) The Bottom Line WrestleMania 42 no longer requires a traditional pay-per-view purchase, but it isn’t completely free either. Fans in the United States will need access to ESPN Unlimited—either through a direct subscription or a participating TV provider—to watch WWE’s biggest event of the year. Internationally, WrestleMania 42 will stream on Netflix, depending on region. This page may contain affiliate links to legal sports betting or fantasy sports partners. If you sign up, Athlon Sports and The Arena Group may be compensated at no cost to you. Read more about Sports Betting on Athlon Sports.About the authorSteven Harrison is a lifelong WWE fan and experienced writer who brings both creativity and analysis to his work, offering a unique spin on wrestling news and concepts.",
